    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d285-a4">

                <pb facs="0577" n="481" xml:id="pg481"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 4 in No. 472,]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Lord Granville to General Schenck.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Foreign Office</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1873-07-31"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 31,
                        1873</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to my note of the 2d ultimo
                    as to the deportation of released convicts and paupers from this country to the
                    United States, I have the honor to transmit to you herewith, for your
                    information, a copy of a letter from the Irish government, with the accompanying
                    reports from the Irish convict-prisons and local government board departments,
                    upon this subject, which I have received from Her Majesty’s secretary of state
                    for the home department.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>GRANVILLE.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
